  "question": {
    "text": "If Rydberg's constant is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>, the longest wavelength of radiation in Paschen series will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo></math>______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "144",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the Paschen radiation series, the longest wavelength corresponds to the transition between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>The formula for the wavelength in the given transition can be written as, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>9</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>16</mn></mstyle></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>R</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>144</mn><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p> Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>144</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}